      "description": "GRADE, and the first content in smart-kg. Certainty-of-evidence grading belongs to WHO L1 guideline development rather than to an agent framework: a folio formalising mathematics has evidence and no use for GRADE. Separated so the extraction is literal — smart-kg/ lifts out whole — which is the layout #223 asks for and bootstrap/ already demonstrates, and it is why this path is repository-scoped, like the bootstrap entry, rather than instance-relative. It has a slot waiting rather than needing one built: evidence-retrieval.bpmn runs Task_AppraiseGrade against \"the grading system the folio declares\", and its own documentation calls that a STRAWPERSON. Adopting the method as a sub-graph keeps the slot pluggable instead of wiring one system into the diagram.",
